  "body": "Reported by the maintainer (2026-11-14, in chat): \"all passes should have Arc Turns at corners as an option when the operation is a type like pocket, slot, etc etc.\"\n\nWhat happens: the passes of the area operations (Pocket, Slot and the same kind of operation) have sharp corners. The operation has no option to make the tool turn a corner on an arc.\n\nExpected:\n- Each operation of this kind has an option for arc turns at the corners of its passes, with a radius parameter.\n- With the option on, the tool moves through a corner on an arc that is tangent to the two moves. The post writes the arc as `G2` or `G3` where the post supports arcs.\n- The default keeps the output of existing programs. The worker lists the operation kinds that get the option in the PR.\n\nSafety: an arc turn changes the toolpath. The arc must stay on the air side of the wall and inside the cut region. The gouge check must judge the result. Material that an arc turn leaves in a corner must not be left silently: the operation must cut it or report it.\n\nDone means: the option and the radius are operation parameters, set through the undoable parameter command and the MCP tool `edit_operation`; a toolpath test for each operation kind pins that the corners are tangent arcs of the given radius; a test pins that no arc cuts past the wall; the default output of existing golden programs does not change.\n",
